(348788, 27611, 4285, '<td valign="top">Railway ties. Actually it''s dangerous to burn those, the cresote is carcenogenic. 6</td>', 'Railway ties. Actually it''s dangerous to burn those, the cresote is carcenogenic. 6', '2003-07-07 07:37:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(348796, 27096, 3080, '<td valign="top">Cute.  The flowers look a little out of focus, but the ship is in good focus and quite funny.  I like how you placed the most obvious object off center in the upper left of the photo.  Good lighting and makes me wonder. ~Heather~</td>', 'Cute.  The flowers look a little out of focus, but the ship is in good focus and quite funny.  I like how you placed the most obvious object off center in the upper left of the photo.  Good lighting and makes me wonder. ~Heather~', '2003-07-07 08:02:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(348798, 27630, 3080, '<td valign="top">I like the crop.  This definately makes me go "hmm?"  I do really like the lighting and how it lights up only part of the person creating some dramatic lighting.  I think not being able to see the entire subject gives this the mystery.  Also, What IS the lighting?  It is a religious thing, or an alien thing?  Definately leaves some questions unanswered for me.  Great shot. ~Heather~</td>', 'I like the crop.  This definately makes me go "hmm?"  I do really like the lighting and how it lights up only part of the person creating some dramatic lighting.  I think not being able to see the entire subject gives this the mystery.  Also, What IS the lighting?  It is a religious thing, or an alien thing?  Definately leaves some questions unanswered for me.  Great shot. ~Heather~', '2003-07-07 08:05:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(348799, 27565, 3080, '<td valign="top">Looking at this shot...I do not think "what happened 9/11" at all.  However, it does make me think "what the hell?" so it does leave unanswered questions.  I can''t tell if this is suposed to be poking fun at a certain group of people or not.  My first impression is that it is, and that seems to be a bold move on  your part.  One that I dont really approve of.  If not though, I still don''t get it.  Which is a good thing in this challenge.  The bearded woman bothers me. ~Heather~</td>', 'Looking at this shot...I do not think "what happened 9/11" at all.  However, it does make me think "what the hell?" so it does leave unanswered questions.  I can''t tell if this is suposed to be poking fun at a certain group of people or not.  My first impression is that it is, and that seems to be a bold move on  your part.  One that I dont really approve of.  If not though, I still don''t get it.  Which is a good thing in this challenge.  The bearded woman bothers me. ~Heather~', '2003-07-07 08:09:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(348802, 27609, 3080, '<td valign="top">Without the title, I''m thinking this is just another shot of some girl in a bikini at the beach.  With your title though I''m thinking that maybe she dropped something into the water and is looking for it?  The focus here is really blurry.  Also, the  horizontal water line chops her head right off.  I think it would habe been better to see that horizon in a different spot.  Not sure if it''s the focus or the lighting, but something is drawing the detail right our of her face.  Would like some more clarity there. ~Heather~</td>', 'Without the title, I''m thinking this is just another shot of some girl in a bikini at the beach.  With your title though I''m thinking that maybe she dropped something into the water and is looking for it?  The focus here is really blurry.  Also, the  horizontal water line chops her head right off.  I think it would habe been better to see that horizon in a different spot.  Not sure if it''s the focus or the lighting, but something is drawing the detail right our of her face.  Would like some more clarity there. ~Heather~', '2003-07-07 08:26:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(348803, 27688, 3080, '<td valign="top">Cute.  I like how you caught the piece in the birds mouth.  Kind of answers the question of "who''s been eating the cats food".   The focus on the food and the birds legs is good.  Looks like he was moving his head a bit though cause the piece in his mouth is a little on the soft focus side.  otherwise, it''s a nice shot. ~Heather~</td>', 'Cute.  I like how you caught the piece in the birds mouth.  Kind of answers the question of "who''s been eating the cats food".   The focus on the food and the birds legs is good.  Looks like he was moving his head a bit though cause the piece in his mouth is a little on the soft focus side.  otherwise, it''s a nice shot. ~Heather~', '2003-07-07 08:28:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(348804, 27654, 3080, '<td valign="top">i''m not really sure this raises any questions in my mind.  Looking at it, with my limited knowledge of hilicopters, this looks to be a guy, who looks like maybe a mechanic taking a break on top of this helicopter.  The shadow that makes him look like he''s got 3 legs kind of bothers me a bit.  The color in the sky is great, and focus and clarity are good as well.  ~Heather~</td>', 'i''m not really sure this raises any questions in my mind.  Looking at it, with my limited knowledge of hilicopters, this looks to be a guy, who looks like maybe a mechanic taking a break on top of this helicopter.  The shadow that makes him look like he''s got 3 legs kind of bothers me a bit.  The color in the sky is great, and focus and clarity are good as well.  ~Heather~', '2003-07-07 08:31:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(348805, 27262, 3080, '<td valign="top">I have no clue what these platforms are used for, so I guess it does raise some questions in my mind.  What are they? Who uses them?  I like the foggy, dark mystery of the photo as well.  I think that adds to the questions.  Had it been totally clear what these were, I don''t think it would have such an effect. ~Heather~</td>', 'I have no clue what these platforms are used for, so I guess it does raise some questions in my mind.  What are they? Who uses them?  I like the foggy, dark mystery of the photo as well.  I think that adds to the questions.  Had it been totally clear what these were, I don''t think it would have such an effect. ~Heather~', '2003-07-07 08:33:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(348806, 27619, 8682, '<td valign="top">wow, wow, wow... The best one of this week. How did you get it?... 10</td>', 'wow, wow, wow... The best one of this week. How did you get it?... 10', '2003-07-07 08:33:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(348807, 27289, 3080, '<td valign="top">The title suggests that the Questions have been answered.  Also, it doesn''t raise any questions in my mind. So I don''t think that it fits the challenge well.   A bird was hit in the road.  Also a very not pleasant subject.  The lighting looks poor, and thank goodness, the focus also seems soft taking away a lot of the detail of your subject.  The background is quite too dark, and overall just not a pleasant shot. ~Heather~</td>', 'The title suggests that the Questions have been answered.  Also, it doesn''t raise any questions in my mind. So I don''t think that it fits the challenge well.   A bird was hit in the road.  Also a very not pleasant subject.  The lighting looks poor, and thank goodness, the focus also seems soft taking away a lot of the detail of your subject.  The background is quite too dark, and overall just not a pleasant shot. ~Heather~', '2003-07-07 08:36:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(348808, 27711, 3080, '<td valign="top">On my monitor, the shadowy areas are kind of blotchy.  I don''t count off for that, cause it could just as easily be my monitor as it could be yours, but just thought I"d mention it.  Focus and clarity are really good.  I like the dramatic lighting, and this definately portrays someone who appears to need some answers.  I think you did a good job with this.  Angle and framing/cropping are also good.  Like how you have some blank space in the area the person is looking toward. ~Heather~</td>', 'On my monitor, the shadowy areas are kind of blotchy.  I don''t count off for that, cause it could just as easily be my monitor as it could be yours, but just thought I"d mention it.  Focus and clarity are really good.  I like the dramatic lighting, and this definately portrays someone who appears to need some answers.  I think you did a good job with this.  Angle and framing/cropping are also good.  Like how you have some blank space in the area the person is looking toward. ~Heather~', '2003-07-07 08:38:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(348809, 27657, 3080, '<td valign="top">This leaves me thinking "what the heck was this guy thinking".  so good for the unanswered questions theme.  Colors are nice and bright, and the background works nicely.  Had it been anything other than a single colored wall, I think it would have made this way too busy.  The angle and framing/cropping are ok.  I like to see the head of the guitar, but that''s just my personal preference.  Focus and clarity are good...interesting shot. ~Heather~</td>', 'This leaves me thinking "what the heck was this guy thinking".  so good for the unanswered questions theme.  Colors are nice and bright, and the background works nicely.  Had it been anything other than a single colored wall, I think it would have made this way too busy.  The angle and framing/cropping are ok.  I like to see the head of the guitar, but that''s just my personal preference.  Focus and clarity are good...interesting shot. ~Heather~', '2003-07-07 08:40:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(348810, 27629, 3080, '<td valign="top">Very nice.  Love the focus and clarity here.  I actually think that the DOF works well too.  Don''t need to see the whole print, but you have the main loop in the print nicely focused.  I can''t tell what the print is on, so that adds to the mystery.  I like the addition of the shiny blue surface.  Adds enough color to make it interesting, but not too much to distract.  Great shot. ~Heather~</td>', 'Very nice.  Love the focus and clarity here.  I actually think that the DOF works well too.  Don''t need to see the whole print, but you have the main loop in the print nicely focused.  I can''t tell what the print is on, so that adds to the mystery.  I like the addition of the shiny blue surface.  Adds enough color to make it interesting, but not too much to distract.  Great shot. ~Heather~', '2003-07-07 08:42:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(348812, 27497, 3080, '<td valign="top">I can''t really see them well to tell if they are tubes or paper, or cloth.   I wonder if we got a closer up shot if it might draw us in a bit more.  Maybe make it a little more interesting.  Your focus and clarity seem ok, I can get a lot of detail in the bark of the tree to the right, just not ont the subject.  I haven''t a clue what it is, which does create the mystery here, but would like to still see it a bit closer up. ~Heather~</td>', 'I can''t really see them well to tell if they are tubes or paper, or cloth.   I wonder if we got a closer up shot if it might draw us in a bit more.  Maybe make it a little more interesting.  Your focus and clarity seem ok, I can get a lot of detail in the bark of the tree to the right, just not ont the subject.  I haven''t a clue what it is, which does create the mystery here, but would like to still see it a bit closer up. ~Heather~', '2003-07-07 08:46:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(348814, 27690, 3080, '<td valign="top">Is the question as to what kind of snake this is?  Or why you have christmas lights up in July? lol.  I think I''d prefer to see the interesting side of the snake.  We can''t really see his head or the lovely pattern on his back.  The underside of him is kind of dark as well, taking away some detail.  Lighting conditions look  a little harsh, as can be seen around the edges of the fingers that are on the sky.  DOF is good to get the house out of the way and make it non distracting, but your house is leaning, so it makes it distracting anyway.  Big snake though.  Definately interesting subject, just not displayed in the most interesting way. ~Heather~</td>', 'Is the question as to what kind of snake this is?  Or why you have christmas lights up in July? lol.  I think I''d prefer to see the interesting side of the snake.  We can''t really see his head or the lovely pattern on his back.  The underside of him is kind of dark as well, taking away some detail.  Lighting conditions look  a little harsh, as can be seen around the edges of the fingers that are on the sky.  DOF is good to get the house out of the way and make it non distracting, but your house is leaning, so it makes it distracting anyway.  Big snake though.  Definately interesting subject, just not displayed in the most interesting way. ~Heather~', '2003-07-07 08:49:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(348822, 27533, 92, '<td valign="top">This makes me want to know more :) The color, compostion and lighting are wonderful !!!! I love the handwritting on the lable. Excellent job ! 10</td>', 'This makes me want to know more :) The color, compostion and lighting are wonderful !!!! I love the handwritting on the lable. Excellent job ! 10', '2003-07-07 09:13:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(348826, 27619, 92, '<td valign="top">I love the blue and white ! The leaning glass, the air bubbles and this makes you wonder... HOW ?????????????????????????? GREAT photo !</td>', 'I love the blue and white ! The leaning glass, the air bubbles and this makes you wonder... HOW ?????????????????????????? GREAT photo !', '2003-07-07 09:17:25.000000', NULL, 1),
