(356176, 27611, 811, '<td valign="top">CRITIQUE CLUB CRITIQUE<br/>by karmat<br/> <br/>Me again.  Actually, I had Club put this back in the pile so someone else could get it, then waited a day, and STILL got it.  Either I am the only one doing cc''s (doubtful) or it is "just meant" for me to critique this picture.  Whichever way it is ----<br/> <br/>Technically, this is a good picture.  The focus is good as you can really see the texture in a lot of the areas, and the grain is visible.  Sometimes it is tempting to oversharpen a shot like this, but this does not seem the case.  The lighting and color tones are good as well.<br/> <br/>Compositionally, I find myself focusing on the hicky-didge in the end of the square rail.  As a result, I am wondering if perhaps, using that as your subject and getting closer wouldn''t have made for a more interesting composition and more of an unanswered question.  If you want to include the entire stack, I think more context is needed to really make the composition stronger.  <br/> <br/>Overall, I think you have a good idea, but it leaves me feeling a little lacking as for the "challenge."  The picture is technically sound and the only thing I would really try to change is the composition. <br/> <br/>Best to you in future challenges.<br/> <br/>Your personal critiquer,<br/>karmat<br/>:-)</td>', 'CRITIQUE CLUB CRITIQUEby karmat Me again.  Actually, I had Club put this back in the pile so someone else could get it, then waited a day, and STILL got it.  Either I am the only one doing cc''s (doubtful) or it is "just meant" for me to critique this picture.  Whichever way it is ---- Technically, this is a good picture.  The focus is good as you can really see the texture in a lot of the areas, and the grain is visible.  Sometimes it is tempting to oversharpen a shot like this, but this does not seem the case.  The lighting and color tones are good as well. Compositionally, I find myself focusing on the hicky-didge in the end of the square rail.  As a result, I am wondering if perhaps, using that as your subject and getting closer wouldn''t have made for a more interesting composition and more of an unanswered question.  If you want to include the entire stack, I think more context is needed to really make the composition stronger.   Overall, I think you have a good idea, but it leaves me feeling a little lacking as for the "challenge."  The picture is technically sound and the only thing I would really try to change is the composition.  Best to you in future challenges. Your personal critiquer,karmat:-)', '2003-07-14 16:14:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(356177, 27667, 811, '<td valign="top">CRITIQUE CLUB CRITIQUE<br/>by karmat<br/> <br/>This picture does meet the challenge, as I think it leaves a lot unsaid, and forces the viewer to wonder about what has happened and why.<br/> <br/>Technically, I like the focus on the bottle and pill with the body being just slightly softer.  I also think the bw gives it a colder feeling (and I see a slightly blue cast which makes it seem even more final).  Though being tilted makes it feel like she and the pills should slide right out of the frame, I do think it adds more interest than a straight horizontal shot.  <br/> <br/>The only thing I would change is the bottle.  Maybe have her holding other pills, or take the label off.  Once the viewer notices that the letters are backwards (at first I thought it was a foreign language) it is really noticeable and seems to take away some of the punch.<br/> <br/>Overall, very well done with little room for improvement.<br/> <br/>Best to you in future challenges. <br/> <br/>karmat</td>', 'CRITIQUE CLUB CRITIQUEby karmat This picture does meet the challenge, as I think it leaves a lot unsaid, and forces the viewer to wonder about what has happened and why. Technically, I like the focus on the bottle and pill with the body being just slightly softer.  I also think the bw gives it a colder feeling (and I see a slightly blue cast which makes it seem even more final).  Though being tilted makes it feel like she and the pills should slide right out of the frame, I do think it adds more interest than a straight horizontal shot.   The only thing I would change is the bottle.  Maybe have her holding other pills, or take the label off.  Once the viewer notices that the letters are backwards (at first I thought it was a foreign language) it is really noticeable and seems to take away some of the punch. Overall, very well done with little room for improvement. Best to you in future challenges.  karmat', '2003-07-14 16:18:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(356194, 27705, 2752, '<td valign="top">Thanks to all for taking the time to comment.</td>', 'Thanks to all for taking the time to comment.', '2003-07-14 16:35:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(356210, 27676, 6202, '<td valign="top">Critique Club<br/> <br/>Very nice representation of unanswered questions.  I like the way the eye forced to follow the maze of the steps and it makes you wonder where they lead as the disappear out of the image.  <br/> <br/>Your lighting here isn''t bad but could be slightly brighter, the shadows take away from the steps.<br/> <br/>It is overall very nice.  It is nicely done keep up the good work.<br/> <br/>Anna</td>', 'Critique Club Very nice representation of unanswered questions.  I like the way the eye forced to follow the maze of the steps and it makes you wonder where they lead as the disappear out of the image.   Your lighting here isn''t bad but could be slightly brighter, the shadows take away from the steps. It is overall very nice.  It is nicely done keep up the good work. Anna', '2003-07-14 17:08:34.000000', NULL, 0),
